<title>INDIA: Indian soybean up, meal, oil down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean up, meal, oil down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were up by 100-150 rupees per tonne in plant delivery condition but prices were down 100 rupees per tonne in central Indian markets on Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Arrivals were limited due to the marriage season, and farmers will bring their produce to market by the end of the week. Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were low on increased supply from plants and refineries. Soyoil solvent was down 300 rupees and soyoil refined down 100 rupees per tonne. Business was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were slightly decreased as export demand was poor. Soymeal yellow was $325-326 per tonne FAS (Free alongside Ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $129-130 per tonne FAS in bulk for export and was 4,450-4,475 per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business volume was very dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
